      "writtenOn": "2026-06-22T23:25:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I’ve updated the CL description to stay more ambiguous w.r.t. future of this flag.\n\nAck - thanks.\n\n\u003e Do you have any thoughts on the `finish_decoding` fix being gated by this \"for_android\" flag too? I’ve done that initially out of caution to avoid breaking downstream callers, but perhaps this one is OK to do unflagged?\n\nYeah, I was wondering about this as well.  I think that unconditionally calling `finish_decoding` should have quite a small risk - mostly related to the performance or stability cost of processing PNG chunks between the last `IDAT` (or `fdAT`) chunk and `IEND` chunk (there may be some `itXT` or similar chunks).\n\nBut maybe this risk can be reduced even further by moving the `finish_decoding` call from `incrementalDecode` (and/or `incrementalDecodeXForm`) to the destructor of `SkPngRustCodec` (the former may be called once per each animation loop, but the latter only once).  I haven\u0027t worked with this code in a long time, so I am not 100% sure, but I _think_ that `fFrameAtCurrentStreamPosition` can still be used for `isLastFrame`-like checks (even when not inside/actively decoding a frame).\n\nPS. Leaving this as unresolved so you see this comment, but I guess this is not blocking and can be addressed in a follow-up CL (since for now this behavior is Android-only).",
