      "side": 1,
      "message": "This LGTM, but I wanted to share some context FYI - feel free to just ack this comment and move on.\n\nIn theory animation frames can be read in any order and having a `Seek` ability could avoid sequential scanning here: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/codec/SkPngRustCodec.cpp;l\u003d535-537;drc\u003dec7a1e1ff8797407185211eb64151b1bee15bc3a.  OTOH, we launched Rust PNG in Chromium as-is (i.e. with sequential scanning), so maybe the `Seek` bound is indeed unnecessary.",
